 "best_diff": "--- initial\n+++ best\n@@ -19,7 +19,24 @@\n     features (they are standardized and a bias is added), so nonlinear structure only\n     helps if a feature expresses it. Only the Python standard library may be used.\n \n-    Current method: the raw inputs.\n+    Enhanced method: raw inputs plus transformations.\n     \"\"\"\n-    return list(row)\n+    x1, x2, x3, x4, x5, x6 = row\n+    \n+    # Raw inputs plus squares of uniform inputs x4 and x5\n+    f = [x1, x2, x3, x4, x4**2, x5, x5**2, x6]\n+    \n+    # Log transform for skewed input x3\n+    f.append(math.log(x3))\n+    \n+    # Pairwise interaction features\n+    f.append(x1 * x2)\n+    f.append(x1 * x6)\n+    f.append(x2 * x6)\n+    f.append(x6 * math.log(x3))\n+    T = 0.0 # Hard indicator threshold\n+    # Hard indicator feature for x4 > T\n+    f.append(1.0 if x4 > T else 0.0)\n+    \n+    return f\n # OMEGA-BLOCK-END\n",
